"Unless you make minor changes, like fixing a typo, we do not recommend using "
"the GitHub web editor to edit the Rebel Engine API's XML."
msgstr ""

#: contributing/updating_the_api_documentation.rst:42
msgid ""
"It lacks features to edit XML well, like keeping indentations consistent, "
"and it does not allow amending commits based on reviews."
msgstr ""

#: contributing/updating_the_api_documentation.rst:44
msgid ""
"Also, it doesn't allow you to test your changes in the engine or with "
"validation scripts as described in :ref:`contributing/api_writing_guidelines:"
"how to edit class xml`."
msgstr ""

#: contributing/updating_the_api_documentation.rst:49
msgid "Updating the documentation template"
msgstr ""

#: contributing/updating_the_api_documentation.rst:51
msgid ""
"When you create a new class or modify the engine's API, you need to re-"
"generate the XML files in ``docs/``."
