msgstr ""
"Em seguida é a própria luz (`light.png <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/"
"godotengine/godot-demo-projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/light.png>`_). "
"Se clicar na ligação, notará o quão grande ele é. A imagem que usa para uma "
"luz deve cobrir a área que deseja que a sua luz cubra. Esta imagem tem "
"1024x1024 pixels, então deve usá-la para cobrir 1024x1024 pixels no seu jogo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:33
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Lastly, we have the spotlight image: spot.png. The demo uses a blob to show "
"where the light is and the larger light image to show the effect of the "
"light upon the rest of the scene."
msgstr ""
"Por último, temos a imagem do holofote (`spot.png <https://raw."
"githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/master/2d/"
"lights_and_shadows/spot.png>`_). A demo usa um círculo para mostrar onde a "
"luz é e usa a imagem de luz maior para mostrar o efeito da luz sobre o resto "
"da cena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:40
msgid "The demo uses four different nodes:"
msgstr "A demo usa quatro nós diferentes:"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:41
msgid ":ref:`CanvasModulate <class_CanvasModulate>`"
msgstr ":ref:`CanvasModulate <class_CanvasModulate>`"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:42
msgid ":ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>`"
msgstr ":ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>`"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>`"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:46
msgid ""
":ref:`CanvasModulate<class_CanvasModulate>` is used to darken the scene."
msgstr ""
":ref:`CanvasModulate<class_CanvasModulate>` é usado para escurecer a cena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:48
msgid ""
":ref:`Sprites <class_Sprite>` are used to display the textures for the light "
"blobs, the background, and for the shadow casters."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Sprites <class_Sprite>` são usados para exibir as texturas para os "
"pontos de luz, o plano de fundo e para os geradores de sombras."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:51
msgid ""
":ref:`Light2Ds <class_Light2D>` are used to light the scene. The way a light "
"typically works is by adding a selected texture over the rest of the scene "
"to simulate lighting. But it can be used in other ways, for example masking "
"out parts of the scene."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Light2Ds <class_Light2D>` são usados para iluminar a cena. A maneira "
"como uma luz normalmente funciona é adicionando uma textura selecionada "
"sobre o restante da cena para simular a iluminação. Mas pode ser usado de "
"outras maneiras, por exemplo, mascarando partes da cena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:55
msgid ""
":ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>` are used to tell the shader "
"which parts of the scene cast shadows. The shadows appear only on areas "
"covered by the :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>` and their direction is based "
"on the center of the :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`."
msgstr ""
":ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>` são usados para dizer ao "
"shader quais partes da cena projetam sombras. As sombras aparecem apenas nas "
"áreas cobertas pela :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>` e a sua direção é baseada "
"no centro da :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:60
#: tutorials/3d/introduction_to_3d.rst:218
#: tutorials/performance/batching.rst:149
msgid "Lights"
msgstr "Luzes"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:62
msgid ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` cover the entire extent of their respective "
"Texture. They use additive blending to add the color of their texture to the "
"scene."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Luzes <class_Light2D>` cobrem toda a extensão de as suas respetivas "
"Texturas. Usam uma mistura aditiva para adicionar a cor da sua textura à "
"cena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:67
msgid ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` have four ``Modes``: ``Add``, ``Sub``, "
"``Mix``, and ``Mask``."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` tem quatro ``Modes``: ``Add``, ``Sub``, "
"``Mix`` e ``Mask``."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:69
msgid ""
"``Add`` adds the color of the light texture to the scene. It brightens the "
"area under the light."
msgstr ""
"``Add`` adiciona a cor da textura de luz à cena. Ele ilumina a área sob a "
"luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:71
msgid ""
"``Sub`` subtracts the color of the light from the scene. It darkens the area "
"under the light."
msgstr "``Sub`` subtrai a cor da luz da cena. Escurece a área sob a luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:73
msgid ""
"``Mix`` mixes the color of the light with the underlying scene. The "
"resulting brightness is halfway between the color of the light and the color "
"underneath."
msgstr ""
"``Mix`` mistura a cor da luz com a cena subjacente. O brilho resultante está "
"a meio caminho entre a cor da luz e a cor por baixo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:76
msgid ""
"``Mask`` is used to mask out areas that are covered by the light. Masked out "
"areas are hidden or revealed based on the color of the light."
msgstr ""
"``Mask`` é usado para mascarar áreas que são cobertas pela luz. As áreas "
"mascaradas são ocultadas ou reveladas com base na cor da luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:79
msgid ""
"For the demo the lights have two components, the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` itself (which is the effect of the light), and a :ref:"
"`Sprite <class_Sprite>` blob which is an image showing the location of the "
"light source. A child :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` is not necessary to make "
"a :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` work."
msgstr ""
"Para a demonstração, as luzes têm dois componentes, o :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` em si (que é o efeito da luz) e um :ref:`Sprite "
"<class_Sprite>` blob que é uma imagem mostrando a localização de a fonte de "
"luz. Um filho :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` não é necessário para fazer um :"
"ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` funcionar."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:87
msgid "Shadows"
msgstr "Sombras"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:89
msgid ""
"Shadows are made by intersecting a :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` with a :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`."
msgstr ""
"As sombras são feitas cruzando uma :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` com uma :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:91
msgid ""
"By default shadows are turned off. To turn them on click on the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` and under the Shadows section check ``Enabled``."
msgstr ""
"Por sombras padrão são desligadas. Para ligá-los clique no :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` e sob a secção Shadows marque ``Ativado```."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:94
msgid ""
"In the demo we are using a :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` with a Texture on it "
"to make the \"Shadow Casters\", but in reality all you need is a couple of :"
"ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>`. By itself the :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>` looks like a dark spot and in this "
"demo the :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` is just a black square."
msgstr ""
"Na demo, estamos usando um :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` com uma Textura para "
"fazer os \"Shadow Casters\", mas na realidade tudo o que precisa é um par "
"de :ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>`. Por si só, o :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>` parece um ponto escuro e nesta "
"demonstração o :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` é apenas um quadrado preto."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:102
msgid ""
"Now that we have covered the basics of the nodes being used, we can now walk "
"step by step through the process of making a scene like the one found in the "
"demo."
msgstr ""
"Agora que abordamos os fundamentos dos nós usados, agora podemos percorrer "
"passo a passo o processo de criação de uma cena como a encontrada na demo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:105
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First add a :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` and set its texture to the "
"background image. For your game this can be any background you choose. For "
"this style of shadow it is most likely to be a floor texture."
msgstr ""
"Primeiro adicione um :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` e defina a sua textura "
"para a `imagem de fundo <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-"
"demo-projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/background.png> `_. Para o seu "
"jogo, pode ser qualquer plano de fundo que escolher. Para este estilo de "
"sombra, é mais provável que seja uma textura de chão."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:111
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next create three :ref:`Light2D's <class_Light2D>` and set their textures to "
"the light image. You can alter their color in the top section. By default "
"shadows are turned off and the ``mode`` is set to ``add``. This means that "
"each light adds its own color to whatever is underneath."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, crie três :ref:`Light2D's <class_Light2D>` e defina as suas "
"texturas para a `imagem de luz <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/"
"godotengine/godot-demo-projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/light.png> `_. "
"Pode alterar a sua cor na secção superior. Por padrão, as sombras são "
"desativadas e o ``mode`` é definido como ``add``. Isso significa que cada "
"luz adiciona a sua própria cor ao que está por baixo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:118
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next add a child :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` to each of the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` nodes, and set the :ref:`Sprite's <class_Sprite>` texture "
"to the blob image. Each of these should stay centered on the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` node. The blob is the image of the light itself while the :"
"ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` shows the effect that the light has on the "
"scene. The :ref:`LightOccluder2D's <class_LightOccluder2D>` will treat the "
"position of the light as the center of the :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` "
"node, which is why we want the blob to be centered on its parent :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>`."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, adicione um filho :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` a cada um dos "
"nós :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` e defina a textura :ref:`Sprite "
"<class_Sprite>` para a imagem `blob <https:/ /raw.githubusercontent.com/"
"godotengine/godot-demo-projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/spot.png>`_. "
"Cada um deles deve ficar centralizado no nó :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`. O "
"blob é a imagem da própria luz enquanto :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` mostra "
"o efeito que a luz tem na cena. O :ref:`LightOccluder2D's "
"<class_LightOccluder2D>` tratará a posição da luz como o centro do nó :ref:"
"`Light <class_Light2D>` e é por isso que queremos que o blob seja "
"centralizado no seu pai :ref:` Luz <class_Light2D>`."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:127
