"texture, ``SCREEN_TEXTURE`` (and ``DEPTH_TEXTURE`` for depth, in the case of "
"3D). It takes as argument the UV of the screen and returns a vec3 RGB with "
"the color. A special built-in varying: SCREEN_UV can be used to obtain the "
"UV for the current fragment. As a result, this simple canvas_item fragment "
"shader:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/screen-reading_shaders.rst:32
msgid "results in an invisible object, because it just shows what lies behind."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/shaders/screen-reading_shaders.rst:34
msgid ""
"The reason why textureLod must be used is because, when Rebel Engine copies "
"back a chunk of the screen, it also does an efficient separatable gaussian "
"blur to its mipmaps."
